lass="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monte-cassino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monte Cassino</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monte Cassino is a hill above Cassino in southern Italy where Benedict of Nursia founded his monastery around 529, the cradle of the Benedictine order.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monte-cavo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monte-cavo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monte Cavo</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monte Cavo is the second-highest peak of the Alban Hills south-east of Rome, rising to about 950 metres above Lake Albano.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monte-cimino"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monte-cimino.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monte Cimino</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monte Cimino is the highest peak, at about 1,050 metres, of the Monti Cimini, a range of extinct volcanoes near Viterbo in northern Lazio, Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monte-naranco"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monte-naranco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monte Naranco</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monte Naranco is a hill overlooking Oviedo in Asturias, northern Spain.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/monte-sannace"><span class="enc-name">Monte Sannace</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monte Sannace is an archaeological site near Gioia del Colle in Apulia, southern Italy, the remains of one of the largest settlements of the Peucetians.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monte-testaccio"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monte-testaccio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monte Testaccio</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monte Testaccio is an artificial hill in Rome, about 35 m high, made almost entirely of broken amphorae discarded between the 1st and 3rd centuries CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monte-titano"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monte-titano.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monte Titano</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monte Titano is a limestone mountain in San Marino, rising to 739 metres, on whose ridge stand the City of San Marino and the republic's Three Towers.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/montego-bay"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/montego-bay.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Montego Bay</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Montego Bay is a city on the north-west coast of Jamaica and the capital of the parish of St James.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monterado"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monterado.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monterado</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monterado is a town in Bengkayang Regency, West Kalimantan, Indonesia, inland from Singkawang.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/montereau-fault-yonne"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/montereau-fault-yonne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Montereau-Fault-Yonne</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Montereau-Fault-Yonne is a town in the Seine-et-Marne department, south-east of Paris, where the Yonne flows into the Seine.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monterey-california"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monterey-california.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monterey, California</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monterey is a city on Monterey Bay on the central coast of California.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monterozzi-necropolis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monterozzi-necropolis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monterozzi necropolis</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Monterozzi necropolis is an Etruscan cemetery on a hill east of Tarquinia in Lazio, Italy, used from the Villanovan period of the 9th century BCE into Roman times.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/monterrey"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/monterrey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Monterrey</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Monterrey is the capital of the state of Nuevo León in north-eastern Mexico.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/montesquieu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/montesquieu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Montesquieu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Montesquieu, Charles-Louis de Secondat, Baron de La Brède et de Montesquieu, was a French magistrate and political philosopher of the Enlightenment.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/montevideo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/montevideo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Montevideo</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Montevideo is the capital and largest city of Uruguay, on the northern shore of the Río de la Plata.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/montferrat"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/montferrat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Montferrat</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Montferrat (Monferrato) is a hilly region of southern Piedmont, Italy, between the Po and the Ligurian Apennines.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/montfort-castle"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/montfort-castle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Montfort Castle</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Montfort Castle is a ruined crusader fortress in the hills of western Upper Galilee, in present-day Israel.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/montgenevre-pass"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/montgenevre-pass.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Montgenèvre Pass</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Montgenèvre Pass is a high pass in the Cottian Alps linking the upper Durance valley in France with the Susa valley in Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/montgomery-bus-boycott"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/montgomery-bus-boycott.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Montgomery bus boycott</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Montgomery bus boycott was a protest campaign against racial segregation on the buses of Montgomery, Alabama, and a foundational event of the civil rights movement.</span></a></li></ul>
